      "path": "src/coordinators/daily-review/daily-review.ts",
      "content": "The owed group now contributes blocking reasons, but `nextTaskOf` still receives only walked Trade IDs and walked due debts. For example, saving the last walked Trade's Action while T-M still has a due Close Review returns `completion.kind === 'Incomplete'` together with `nextStep.kind === 'Done'`. Post-save callers are expected to continue directly from this result, so they are told to stop before the remaining obligation is resolved. Include due owed-group cards in next-task selection after the walk (and support loading those cards), with a regression test for saving the last walked card while an outside-walk reflection remains due.",
      "existing_code": "      review: { reviewDate, cutoff, families, owed: group.trades, completion },",
      "start_line": 422,
      "end_line": 422,
      "category": "bug",
      "severity": "medium"
    },
    {
      "path": "src/domain/journal-debt/index.ts",
      "content": "This adds a nested ternary, which is explicitly disallowed by the review checklist. Use an equality guard followed by a single comparison ternary to preserve the same identity ordering.",
